  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Book an impairment and clear it when the books are whole again.\\n\\nUSDC (`usdc_pt_charge`): the missing USDC pTokens are a backstop loss: Bs.ptokens and\\nLedger(USDC) both drop by the charge (BadAmount if either is smaller). The rule\\nLedger(USDC) = held + Bs.ptokens + claims keeps holding, so no later ledger_sub underflows.\\n\\nXLM (`xlm_pt_restore`, WP4 25 Nov): the backstop holds no XLM pTokens, so an XLM deficit\\ncannot be booked against it, and a Ledger-only write-down would leave Ledger(XLM) below\\nheld + claims (the last XLM closer's ledger_sub and pToken transfer would fail). Instead\\nthe admin RESTORES XLM pTokens: `xlm_pt_restore` pTokens move admin -> contract and\\nLedger(XLM) is unchanged. (Anyone may also restore by plain transfer: surpluses are\\nignored.) Backstop-funded XLM restoration (USDC -> XLM swap) is an open owner decision.\\n\\nClears Impaired only if, afterwards, Ledger <= balance for both markets AND the backstop\\nis not exhausted (nav_pt(false) >= 0; recapitalise with admin_recapitalize first). The\\nN",
      "name": "admin_resolve_impairment",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "admin",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "usdc_pt_charge",
          "type_": "u128"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "xlm_pt_restore",
          "type_": "u128"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": []
    }
  }
